sections.wikitext:
{{Blockquote|text="Calm Down" is all about the events that led me to finding love at the time. It started at a party where I saw a girl who stood out from other girls so I felt like shooting my shot. We spoke and danced... but her friends didn't let me get any closer which killed the vibe, but afterwards when they weren't there, we stayed in touch and hit it off.|author=Rema on how the song came about|source=''[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]''<ref>{{cite web|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/rema-announces-debut-album-rave-and-roses-shares-new-song-calm-down-listen/|title=Rema Announces Debut Album Rave & Roses, Shares New Song "Calm Down": Listen|last=Minsker|first=Evan|website=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]|date=10 February 2022|access-date=28 August 2022|archive-date=25 March 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220325030014/https://pitchfork.com/news/rema-announces-debut-album-rave-and-roses-shares-new-song-calm-down-listen/|url-status=live}}</ref>}}

Miami-based Amanda Ibanez, who also goes by her stage name Kiddo AI, was asked by Interscope senior director of A&R Vanessa Angiuli to write a spec verse
for Selena Gomez on the song. Ibanez quickly wrote and recorded two different possible options for a Selena verse. Within a few hours of sending them to Angiuli, Ibanez received a response back from Angiuli who told her that Gomez loved the verse. Within the next few weeks, Ibanez and Gomez began to trade ideas back and forth and refine the verse. Ibanez eventually flew to Los Angeles to complete the song after a request to have more of Gomez on the song.<ref name="variety">{{cite magazine|url=https://variety.com/2023/music/news/kiddo-ai-selena-gomez-verse-calm-down-1235556950/|title=Hitmaker of the Month: From Watching 'Wizards of Waverly Place' to Writing for Selena Gomez, How Kiddo A.I. Got Her Big Break|last=Wass|first=Mike|magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=16 March 2023|access-date=19 September 2023|archive-date=15 September 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230915160423/https://variety.com/2023/music/news/kiddo-ai-selena-gomez-verse-calm-down-1235556950/|url-status=live}}</ref>

{{Blockquote|text=Like most girls my age, I grew up watching Selena on ''[[Wizards of Waverly Place]]'' and always admired her demeanor of being so classy and collected. So the first line is, 'I know I look shy, but for you I get down,' and I thought that that would be kind of fun for her to say, because she's so proper, I feel, from the outside. I just wanted her to feel herself a little bit.|author=Amanda Ibanez on channeling Gomez to write her verse|source=<ref name="variety" />}}

The song was described as a "vibey"<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/selena-gomez-rema-calm-down-1234582206/|title=Hear Selena Gomez Join Afrorave Artist Rema on Reworked Single 'Calm Down'|last=Zemler|first=Emily|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|date=26 August 2022|access-date=28 August 2022|archive-date=28 August 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220828021312/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/selena-gomez-rema-calm-down-1234582206/|url-status=live}}</ref> "feelgood smash hit".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.thefader.com/2022/08/26/selena-gomez-rema-calm-down-remix|title=Selena Gomez joins Rema on "Calm Down" remix|last=Renshaw|first=David|website=[[The Fader]]|date=26 August 2022|access-date=28 August 2022|archive-date=28 August 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220828005141/https://www.thefader.com/2022/08/26/selena-gomez-rema-calm-down-remix|url-status=live}}</ref> Reviewing the remix, ''[[Vanguard (Nigeria)|Vanguard]]'' writer Adegboyega Remmy Adeleye thought Gomez' "melodic tune complements Rema's vibe perfectly, maintaining the same energy as the original release".<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.vanguardngr.com/2022/08/review-selena-gomezs-melodic-tune-complements-remas-vibe-for-calm-down-remix/|location=Lagos, Nigeria|title=Review: Selena Gomez's melodic tune complements Rema's vibe for 'Calm Down' remix|last=Adeleye|first=Adegboyega Remmy|newspaper=[[Vanguard (Nigeria)|Vanguard]]|date=26 August 2022|access-date=28 August 2022|archive-date=27 August 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827175213/https://www.vanguardngr.com/2022/08/review-selena-gomezs-melodic-tune-complements-remas-vibe-for-calm-down-remix/|url-status=live}}</ref>

The song is recorded in the key of [[B major]] with a tempo of 107 beats per minute in [[Time signature|common time]].  It follows a chord progression of E–B, and the vocals span from D{{sharp}}<sub>4</sub> to F{{sharp}}<sub>5</sub>.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Gomez |first1=Selena |last2=Ikubor |first2=Divine |last3=Uwaifo |first3=Alexandre |last4=Hunter |first4=Michael |title=Calm Down |url=https://www.musicnotes.com/sheetmusic/mtd.asp?ppn=MN0269588 |website=Musicnotes.com |access-date=17 September 2023 |language=en |date=3 February 2023 |archive-date=6 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231006164046/https://www.musicnotes.com/sheetmusic/mtd.asp?ppn=MN0269588 |url-status=live }}</ref>

sections.text:
{{Blockquote|text="Calm Down" is all about the events that led me to finding love at the time. It started at a party where I saw a girl who stood out from other girls so I felt like shooting my shot. We spoke and danced... but her friends didn't let me get any closer which killed the vibe, but afterwards when they weren't there, we stayed in touch and hit it off.|author=Rema on how the song came about|source=Pitchfork}}

Miami-based Amanda Ibanez, who also goes by her stage name Kiddo AI, was asked by Interscope senior director of A&R Vanessa Angiuli to write a spec verse
for Selena Gomez on the song. Ibanez quickly wrote and recorded two different possible options for a Selena verse. Within a few hours of sending them to Angiuli, Ibanez received a response back from Angiuli who told her that Gomez loved the verse. Within the next few weeks, Ibanez and Gomez began to trade ideas back and forth and refine the verse. Ibanez eventually flew to Los Angeles to complete the song after a request to have more of Gomez on the song.

{{Blockquote|text=Like most girls my age, I grew up watching Selena on Wizards of Waverly Place and always admired her demeanor of being so classy and collected. So the first line is, 'I know I look shy, but for you I get down,' and I thought that that would be kind of fun for her to say, because she's so proper, I feel, from the outside. I just wanted her to feel herself a little bit.|author=Amanda Ibanez on channeling Gomez to write her verse|source=}}

The song was described as a "vibey" "feelgood smash hit". Reviewing the remix, Vanguard writer Adegboyega Remmy Adeleye thought Gomez' "melodic tune complements Rema's vibe perfectly, maintaining the same energy as the original release".

The song is recorded in the key of B major with a tempo of 107 beats per minute in common time.  It follows a chord progression of E–B, and the vocals span from D{{sharp}}<sub>4</sub> to F{{sharp}}<sub>5</sub>.

